    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0832" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.AD1/9: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vincent</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-18T10:00:00+07:00">March 18, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:21 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>389. With reference to Department’s 310, March 8, 9 p.m.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d731-f1"/> Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d731-f2"/> has informed me orally that the Chinese Government
                    accepts the invitation to the proposed conference and that such suggestions and
                    comments as it may have to make will be communicated separately on a subsequent
                    date or be incorporated in the instructions of the delegates for communication
                    when they arrive in Washington. Unofficially he stated that the delegation would
                    probably be composed of seven or eight men and that every effort would be made
                    to have them arrive in Washington by April 27, April 5 having been set as the
                    deadline for preparation for their departure from Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vincent</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
